      "What follows is an intentionally unsettling invitation into a revolutionary vision of deliverance. Jesus was— and remains— a figure who divides the room. Every miracle, every healing, every exorcism carried both offense and freedom in equal measure. His birth, His death, His resurrection all moved in the rhythm Paul called foolishness— the strange wisdom by which God chooses the low, the despised, and the dismissed to dismantle the structures of the wise.",
      "> “‘I thank You, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, that You have hidden these things from the wise and prudent and have revealed them to babes.’”",
