      "## CAPTIVITY CAPTIVE",
      "> “From within, out of the hearts of men, proceed evil thoughts, adulteries, fornications, murders, thefts, covetousness, wickedness, deceit, lewdness, an evil eye, blasphemy, pride, foolishness. All these evil things come from within and defile a man.” ||| MARK 7:21–23",
      "Matthew 15:19 echoes the same truth that the heart is the source of both our actions and our defilement. Ecclesiastes 9:3 adds, “Truly the hearts of the sons of men are full of evil; madness is in their hearts while they live, and after that they go to the dead.” But why is this so? Romans 8:7–8 explains: “The carnal mind is enmity against God; it is not subject to the law of God, nor indeed can be. Those who are in the flesh cannot please God.”",
      "[[img:/images/book/exiting-the-matrix-p167-266.jpg|Matthew 15:19 echoes the same truth that]]",
      "But Scripture also offers hope. Romans 8:3–5 shows the way forward: “What the law could not do, in that it was weak through the flesh, God did by sending His own Son in the likeness of sinful flesh, on account of sin: He condemned sin in the flesh, so that the righteous requirement of the law might be fulfilled in us, who do not walk according to the flesh but according to the Spirit. For those who live according to the flesh set their minds on the things of the flesh, but those who live according to the Spirit, the things of the Spirit.”",
      "How do we practically live this out? By taking every thought captive and presenting it to God. We do not entertain thoughts, whether seemingly good or bad, in isolation. Every thought is to be brought under obedience to Christ, crucified at the Cross and purified by fire and light through the Spirit. The Cross is the Tree of Life, not the Tree of the Knowledge of Good and Evil. The result is the life described in Jeremiah 17:7–8: “Blessed is the man who trusts in the Lord, and whose hope is the Lord. For he shall be like a tree planted by the waters, which spreads out its roots by the river, and will not fear when heat comes; its leaf will be green, and it will not be anxious in the year of drought, nor will it cease from yielding fruit.”",
      "Faith and obedience root us in the Spirit, transforming our hearts and minds so that we no longer live according to the flesh but flourish in God’s eternal provision.",
      "[[img:/images/book/exiting-the-matrix-p168-268.jpg|Illustration from ORDER]]",
      "## TRAP THAT JACKAL",
      "[[img:/images/book/exiting-the-matrix-p170-271.jpg|Illustration from ORDER]]",
      "You don’t escape the matrix by fighting it, you escape it by becoming aware of it. This is the logic of the sub-contrario Kingdom. The “matrix” is simply the interface of the flesh and the natural world. We don’t take pride in seeing it; we don’t make an identity out of it. We recognize it for what it is: a temporary operating system. The moment we stop mistaking it for ultimate reality, we step into the realm of the Spirit. And that’s where the Word begins to cut, divide, expose, and transform everything.",
      "> “The Word of God is living and powerful… sharper than any two‑edged sword… dividing soul and spirit… discerning the thoughts and intents of the heart. Nothing is hidden from His sight; everything is naked before Him.” ||| HEBREWS 4:11–13",
      "The Word dismantles the interface. It reveals what is flesh, what is spirit, what is fear, what is truth, what is pride, and what is freedom. Before Jesus came, the enemy could move freely, “going to and fro,” operating above and beyond human agency. Humanity had no authority to restrain or confront him. But Christ’s incarnation, death, and resurrection trapped the enemy in the flesh‑realm, confining him to the same arena where you now carry the Spirit of God.",
      "It’s like catching the jackal that keeps eating your chickens: you trap it inside the coop, where it can no longer hide in the darkness or strike from the outside. Only then can you deal with it. That’s what Jesus did. The enemy was brought down and you were raised up. You now have agency. You now have authority. You now stand in Christ, above the powers that once threatened you from beyond your reach. Much like we saw Jesus do when he cast the legion of demons from the man of the Gerasenes into the herd of pigs.",
      "## ILLUMINE TO CONSUME",
      "Every problem you face is not a sign of impending defeat, rather it’s something that has been handed to you because you now have the ability to take it, lay it on the altar, and watch the fire of God consume it. You bring it to the altar of the Cross, not just to the light of the Word, but to the God who is a Consuming Fire. When you offer it up at the altar of the Cross, the light of God’s word exposes it for what it is, and the fire of God consumes it. The smoke that rises from the burnt sacrifices, rises to God as incense. It is a pleasing offering through which His power is made perfect in our weakness, and in return He gives you not just understanding, but transformation. In Christ, you don’t escape reality. You rule over it. You bring everything through the Cross— the true Tree of Life— and whatever passes through its fire emerges purified, healed, and brought back into divine order. Scripture tells us that a flaming sword stands at the entrance to Eden, not as a wall to keep humanity out, but as the refining presence that guides us back in. This living, active Word cuts through illusion and pretense, distinguishing flesh from spirit, exposing the heart’s motives, and consuming everything that cannot belong in God’s restored garden.",
      "> “The words that I speak to you are spirit, and they are life.” ||| JOHN 6:63",
